{"outcome": true, "goal": "  subject: formal_logic\n  question: Select the best English interpretation of the given proposition, using the following translation key: Ax: x is an apartment Hx: x is a house Lx: x is large Bxy: x is bigger than y (∃x)[Hx • (∀y)(Ay ⊃ Bxy)]\n  do not use query-web or semantic-scholar in your reasoning. use generate or think to surface knownledge, or refine to extract information from text.\n  choices:\n    A: Some houses are smaller than all apartments.\n    B: Every house is bigger than every apartment.\n    C: Some apartment is smaller than every house.\n    D: Some houses are bigger than every apartment.\n\n\nRESPONSE INSTRUCTIONS:\noutput your answer in this format:\nANSWER: X\nwhere X is A, B, C, or D.\nFinally, say the answer to User: ", "plan": [{"type": "think", "value": "Let me break down the logical proposition step by step. The proposition is (∃x)[Hx • (∀y)(Ay ⊃ Bxy)]. This is an existential quantifier followed by a conjunction. The first part Hx means 'x is a house'. The second part (∀y)(Ay ⊃ Bxy) is a universal quantifier. For all y, if y is an apartment (Ay), then x is bigger than y (Bxy). So the whole thing says 'There exists an x such that x is a house AND for all y, if y is an apartment, then x is bigger than y'. This means there exists a house such that it is bigger than every apartment. This translates to 'Some houses are bigger than every apartment'."}, {"type": "generate-note", "prompt": "Given the logical proposition (∃x)[Hx • (∀y)(Ay ⊃ Bxy)] and the translation key Ax: x is an apartment, Hx: x is a house, Lx: x is large, Bxy: x is bigger than y, what is the best English interpretation of this proposition? The choices are: A: Some houses are smaller than all apartments. B: Every house is bigger than every apartment. C: Some apartment is smaller than every house. D: Some houses are bigger than every apartment.", "context": "The logical proposition translates to: There exists an x such that x is a house AND for all y, if y is an apartment, then x is bigger than y. This means there exists a house such that it is bigger than every apartment. The correct English interpretation is 'Some houses are bigger than every apartment.'", "out": "$translation_analysis"}], "error_count": 0}
